course: dictionary
lesson: 13681
title: Words that hold things back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inhibit is a verb, and it means to slow something down, block it or stop it from happening or growing. «Salt inhibits bacteria, so it helps keep food fresh for longer.» The salt does not make the bacteria bigger or faster. It holds them back.
explain: Inhibit can also be about people. To feel inhibited is to feel shy or unable to act freely. «Being watched inhibits him, so he cannot draw his best picture.» The clue is watched: something is stopping him from doing his best.
explain: To check your meaning, ask: what is being held back? Then swap in slow down, block or hold back. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Inhibit is a verb: inhibit, inhibits, inhibited, inhibiting.
fact: «Inhibit» means to slow down, block or stop something from happening or growing.
fact: «Inhibited» can mean shy or unable to act freely.
fact: Useful phrases: inhibit growth, feel inhibited.
fact: In science, a substance that inhibits a reaction slows that reaction down.
exercise: «Salt inhibits bacteria.» What does inhibits mean here? | *Slows down or stops | Paints the walls | Warms up the food | Makes bigger and faster
exercise: «Being watched inhibits him.» Which word is closest in meaning to inhibits? | Plays | Dances | Shouts | *Holds back
exercise: Lena said, «I felt inhibited, so I did not sing.» What does inhibited mean? | Very happy and loud | Lost in the woods | Hungry after a long walk | *Shy and unable to act freely
test: «Cold weather inhibits the growth of some plants.» What does inhibits mean here? | Paints the leaves green | *Slows down the growth | Makes the plants taller overnight | Helps the plants grow faster
test: Which word means shy and unable to act freely? | Drooped | Ancient | Luminous | *Inhibited
exam: «The rain inhibited our game, so we stayed inside.» What does inhibited mean here? | Made faster and louder | *Blocked or stopped from happening | Cheered by everyone | Painted on the walls
